<!doctype html>
<!--
  The page a seed lands on.

  Every seed link minted so far points here. With a seed in the fragment this is
  the invitation to grow it; with nothing there it is the page that says what
  Peace Garden is, which is why it is one page rather than two.

  An iPhone with the app installed never sees this: the association file claims
  `/s*`, so iOS opens the app instead. The page therefore addresses a stranger,
  always, and never has to branch on whether the reader already has it.

  Static, and staying that way. No server-side rendering, no analytics, no font
  CDN, no third-party anything. Everything it draws, it draws from the fragment
  and from two files on this origin.

  SEAM — the App Clip. Once the clip target exists, the Safari route to a clip
  card is a `<meta name="apple-itunes-app">` tag on this page. It goes in the
  head below. The association file does not change for it; what changes is the
  App Clip Experience registered against the `/s` prefix in App Store Connect.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Peace Garden makes a plant out of two people meeting. A seed travels in a link, and this is where one lands."
    />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <!--
      The stage, not a web page: the plant stands in a soft pool of light drawn
      in screen space, behind everything, exactly as `StageBackdrop` draws it.
    -->
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page" id="page">
      <header class="masthead">
        <img class="mark" src="/assets/mark.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
        <p class="wordmark heading">Peace Garden</p>
      </header>

      <!-- A seed arrived. -->
      <section class="seed" id="seed" hidden>
        <h1 class="heading" data-s="seedTitle"></h1>

        <div class="stage">
          <!--
            SEAM — the plant.

            This box is where the plant is drawn, at the proportions it is drawn
            at. What fills it is `SeedCore` compiled to WebAssembly, handing a
            WebGL renderer the same buffers `PlantSceneBuilder` gets from
            `PlantBuilder` — positions, normals, UVs and indices grouped by
            material role — so the JavaScript is a renderer and nothing else.
            The open question is bundle size on a phone on mobile data, and the
            fallback if it is too heavy is a JavaScript port of the geometry
            with a CI gate. A third hand-maintained copy with nothing checking
            it is the one option that is off the table. docs/WEBSITE.md §"What
            renders the plant".

            Until then the stage is lit and the ground line is drawn, and the
            plant's name stands where the app puts it.
          -->
          <div class="stage__plant" data-seam="renderer"></div>
          <div class="stage__ground" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        </div>

        <p class="plant-name" id="plant-name"></p>
        <p class="label" id="sent-by"></p>
        <p class="label" id="planted"></p>

        <blockquote class="passage" id="passage">
          <p id="passage-text"></p>
          <footer class="label" id="passage-source"></footer>
        </blockquote>

        <section class="invitation">
          <h2 class="label" data-s="growTitle"></h2>
          <p class="body" data-s="growBody"></p>
          <p class="body quiet" data-s="appNote"></p>
        </section>
      </section>

      <!--
        A link that arrived broken, said in the body voice rather than the
        label voice: a whole sentence tracked out in capitals is a shout, and
        this one is already the least welcome thing on the page.
      -->
      <p class="notice body" id="notice" hidden></p>

      <!-- No seed: what this is. -->
      <section class="about" id="about" hidden>
        <h1 class="plant-name tagline" data-s="tagline"></h1>
        <p class="body" data-s="about1"></p>
        <p class="body" data-s="about2"></p>
        <p class="body quiet" data-s="about3"></p>
      </section>

      <footer class="foot">
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg
              class="chooser__mark"
              viewBox="0 0 16 16"
              aria-hidden="true"
              focusable="false"
            >
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <noscript>
      <p class="body noscript">
        This page reads the seed in your link with JavaScript, in your browser,
        because that is where the seed stays.
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/page.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
